course: dictionary
lesson: 15369
title: The Soviets
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look alike but mean different things, and a capital letter can be a clue. «The Soviets sent the first satellite, Sputnik, into space in 1957.» Here Soviets means the people, government or army of the Soviet Union, a large country that existed from 1922 to 1991.
explain: A small s changes the meaning. «The soviet met in a factory hall in 1917 to choose a leader.» Here soviet means a council of workers or soldiers in Russia around 1917. Soviet is the Russian word for "council".
explain: Look at the words around it. Soviet Union, Soviet times and the Cold War tell you the topic is history. Ask yourself what word would fit: «The soviet met to vote» still makes sense if you swap in "council", so you have found its meaning.
fact: The Soviets means the people, government or army of the Soviet Union.
fact: The Soviet Union was a large country that existed from 1922 to 1991, led from Moscow.
fact: A soviet with a small s was a council of workers or soldiers in Russia around 1917.
fact: The Soviets sent Sputnik into space in 1957 and Yuri Gagarin in 1961.
fact: Many countries in the Soviet Union, such as Ukraine and Belarus, did not choose to join it.
exercise: «The Soviets sent the first satellite, Sputnik, into space in 1957.» Who sent Sputnik into space? | The Romans | *The Soviets | The Vikings
exercise: «The soviet met in a factory hall in 1917.» What does soviet (small s) mean here? | *A council of workers or soldiers | A large country in Europe | A type of heavy machine
exercise: Which country was called the Soviet Union? | Britain, from 1922 to 1991 | Australia, after 1991 | *The USSR, a large country that existed from 1922 to 1991 | A large country that existed from 1922 to 1991
test: «The Soviet Union was led from the city of Moscow.» Where was the Soviet Union led from? | *Moscow | Paris | Berlin | London
test: «Yuri Gagarin became the first person in space in 1961.» Who sent him into space? | The Americans | The French | *The Soviets | The Germans
exam: Which sentence is a true fact about the Soviet Union? | It existed from 1800 to 1850 | It was led from London | It is a country in Africa today | *It existed from 1922 to 1991
